se navigation apps for example here  the google map and apple map can  actually show different route  recommendations to their users  and this actually creates the  information he progenity experienced by  the users of different platforms and can  result in different realized um and  experience the travel time  well people will assess and compare  different apps and then this will result  in their choice of information platforms  and this leads to the equilibrium market  share of these platforms  the question we want to ask here is how  does this heterogeneous information  environment  affects the traveler's choices and the  congestion and how can we assess the  relative value of information for  different users  um so i want to convey the intuition of  this problem through a very simple  example  so we have two  routes in a network so it's a two route  parallel network  why is the highway that may or may not  have an incident when there is an  incident then the cost of the highway  will become higher but otherwise in  nominal state the highway is much  shorter than the deport  so a group of people who use information  platform knows exactly whether there is  an incident while the rest of the people  have no information of the incident  the scenario one is that this  information of incident is only shared  by  a small size of the population  what happens here is that when there is  no incident  the people who have this accurate  information will choose to take the  highway exclusively while the rest of  the people think they do not know and  because of their large sites and to  avoid congestion  some of them will take highway while the  others will take deport  however when there is actually an  incident and the informed population  knows about it they are going to switch  to exclusively take the detour  this allowed informed the population to  exclusively avoid  running into incident and they actually  experience lower cost than the other  population so in this case information  has positive value  on the other hand when information is  shared by a lot of people so the size of  the informed population is very large  the informed population can no longer  exclusively take the highway because of  its large size and the congestion  imposed by people who receive the same  information  as a result both population will split  on both routes in both states incident  or nominal and they actually experience  the same cost due to the congestion  so in this case information has zero  value what i did in this work is  basically to build a general bayesian  congestion gm framework to analyze uh  the impact of  multiple information platforms which  have heterogeneous accuracies levels of  their signals and can be potentially  correlated  um to uh to to assess how the joint  distribution of the signal as the  asymmetric information environment  on the routing behavior the selfish  rotting behavior and the congestion  so here the selfish interaction is  modeled as the bayesian wardrobe  equilibrium of this game  well we have three contributions the  first is the complete characterization  of the bayesian wardrobe equilibrium for  this general network environment and  information environment  the second is that we identify three  regimes as the changes between any  the the using population sizes of any  pair of information platforms and assess  how the relative value of information  can be positive zero or negative  so this reveals the trade-off between  the gain from having this information  versus the congestion externality  imposed by people in the same population  the third is based on the analysis of  relative value of information we analyze  when people are able to choose which  platform they want to use what will be  their choice of information and the  resulting equilibrium market share of  these platforms  well building on these results we can go  one step further to study how to design  the information environment  in order to reduce the overflow of  traffic in small residential area  and because of our analysis of the  relative value of information and choice  of information platform this allows us  to be different from the bayesian the  classical bayesian persuasion literature  in a sense that we allow the travelers  to decide if they want to receive opt-in  of receiving the signals versus opting  out  and in fact even with this flexibility  we show that the optimal information  design  can minimize the traffic overflow and  without sending the signals to all of  the people  well in a second part of multi-agent  learning i go beyond the static setting  and try to really close the loop so the  first part we studied how the  information is affecting the strategic  interaction and the outcome in the  network the system the second part i  closed the loop to study the case when  there is repeated interaction between  the platform and players in a sense that  the data that is used to estimate the  parameter is generated as the outcome of  the  of this strategic game  and this leads to the dynamic interplay  between learning of the unknown  parameter on the platform site  and learning in games with imperfect  information and there is a  repeated  repeated interplay between the two  so this leads to the non-iid data set  that is endogenously generated by the  player strategies  and i developed new tools to study this  dynamic interplay between statistical  learning and strategy learning of the  game the theoretical results we showed  includes the convergence of both the  parameter estimates and strategies  stability properties in terms of the  local and global stability as well as  under what condition this will converge  to complete learning  well the application of this theoretical  tools is to design adaptive tooling  mechanisms so this is one application  that induces socially optimal outcome in  networks with unknown latency function  and what i'm um i'm currently working on  in berkeley is to 